Context
  Asked to have subagents mine the git log for tasks around trace, startup and
  tooling for Guile projects, and turn them into feature requests or a document
  for future skills, evals and a test bed. Four subagents, one per dimension,
  read-only, each required to cite a sha or file:line per claim. Their findings
  are in docs/roadmap.org; nothing was taken on faith where a check was cheap.

Deviations
  Two claims were verified locally instead of being restated, and both changed
  the document. The lint finding (C1) came back from the tooling pass as an
  assertion; planting a broken form confirmed exit 0, so it leads the roadmap.
  The orphan finding was not in any agent's report at all --- it surfaced from
  the post-checks cleanup sweep, and is the one item here measured today rather
  than read out of the record.

  evals/PLAN.org's remaining hydra.lan references were left alone deliberately.
  They carry no address, the IP is already recorded as operator-held and absent
  from the repo (PLAN.org:88), and the FQDN-vs-short-name distinction is the
  whole point of the known_hosts finding: generalizing it would destroy the
  lesson. Only the service inventory was removed.

Considerations
  This branch carries no change under skills/, .claude-plugin/ or scripts/lib/,
  so it is not `deployable' and needs no version bump. The shipped half of this
  work --- redacting an internal endpoint out of the committed benchmark
  artifacts, the SKILL.md wording, and the manifest path fix --- is deliberately
  a separate branch, because merging a deployable PR publishes a release and
  0.1.4 is already claimed by the open PR #4.

  The eleven orphan processes belong to another login (jwalsh) and were left
  running. Reaping them is the user's call, not this branch's.

Timeline
  2026-09-28, nexus, FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE, guile3 3.0.10, direnv 2.35.0, as
  dsp-dr. Branched from main rather than from docs/contributing-check-targets so
  PR #5 stays a single-purpose diff.
